{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"cosmogonal-avoided-zenaida","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## The defect\n\nFound by the ticket-c5b3 sibling sweep after the same bug broke CI there.\n\n`tests/unit/test_audit_ticket_page.py:21` and `tests/unit/test_audit_ticket_page_heldout.py:21`\nboth do:\n\n    from tests.unit import _audit_page_helpers as H  # noqa: E402\n\n`tests` is not an importable package: neither `tests/__init__.py` nor `tests/unit/__init__.py`\nexists. A `tests.`-rooted absolute import therefore only resolves when the repository root\nhappens to be on `sys.path`, which is true under `python -m pytest` (it inserts the cwd) and\nFALSE under the bare `pytest` console script that CI runs. Demonstrated on ticket c5b3 with an\nidentical import:\n\n    pytest tests/unit/metrics/test_scc_module_size_reconciliation_heldout.py\n      -> ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'tests'\n    python -m pytest <same file>\n      -> passes\n\n## Why it is not failing today\n\nIt is MASKED, not correct. Both modules call `pytest.importorskip(\"fastapi\")` and\n`pytest.importorskip(\"httpx\")` on the two lines ABOVE the import (hence the `# noqa: E402`).\nThe `[ui]` extra is absent from the lean CI suite, so the module skips before the broken\nimport line is ever executed. Install the `[ui]` extra and run bare `pytest` and these two\nmodules fail at collection.\n\nThat makes this worse than a plain breakage: the tests read as covered while providing no\ncoverage in exactly the environment where the extra IS present.\n\n## The fix\n\n`_audit_page_helpers.py` lives in `tests/unit/`, the same directory as both importers, so the\nrepo's established same-directory bare-name convention applies:\n\n    from _audit_page_helpers import ...\n\npytest's prepend import mode inserts `tests/unit` into `sys.path` (it is the first ancestor\nwithout an `__init__.py`), so a bare name resolves. Every other bare-name test import in this\nrepo is same-directory like this -- `metrics_polyglot_support`, `reviewbot_convergence_support`,\n`_dc_support`, `test_completion_gate`.\n\nAlternatively, move the helpers to `tests/_audit_page_support.py`: `tests/` is on `sys.path` by\nDELIBERATE guarantee (`tests/conftest.py` inserts it), which is the mechanism c5b3 used for its\ncross-directory case via the new `tests/module_size_support.py`.\n\n## Why it was not fixed inside c5b3\n\nc5b3 is an scc-metrics bug fix. These two files are an unrelated feature area (the audit page,\nstory ff6f), the defect cannot currently fire, and editing them there would have been scope\ncreep on a change already at its third patch set.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Neither audit-page test module uses a `tests.`-rooted import.\n- [ ] Both modules import and collect successfully under BARE `pytest` (not just\n      `python -m pytest`) with the `[ui]` extra installed, verified from a cwd other than the\n      repository root.\n- [ ] A repository-wide check confirms no `tests.`-rooted import remains anywhere under\n      `tests/`; consider a lint rule or a guard test so the pattern cannot return, since the\n      failure is invisible under the common `python -m pytest` invocation.","id":"a371-fb42-32c5-48bd","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"audit-page tests use a 'tests.'-rooted import that cannot resolve under bare pytest"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785918346180424001,"uuid":"748715aa-5b4b-4ec6-a53f-93acbf7423c4"}